  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated, multi-sector emergency response to support themost vulnerable in DeZ</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to provide continuity to Oxfam&apos;s area -based and multi -sectoral humanitarian response in the governorate of Deir Ez Zor, ensuring the access to basic services, strengthening resilience and protection. The project will focus on 3 main sectors: Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), agricultural support and food security, and protection sector, with specific attention to people living with disabilities, reaching a total of 55,385 individuals. The proposal was designed based on the experience gained and lessons learnt in the ongoing AICS project and in consultation with communities and key stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
